K0  controls of the curvature routine: 4|dx|^2/(1 +- |x|^2)^2 has Ric = +-(m-1) g at 0
  [True] m=2, sphere: Ric == 1*(m-1)*g
  [True] m=2, hyperbolic space: Ric == -1*(m-1)*g
  [True] m=3, sphere: Ric == 1*(m-1)*g
  [True] m=3, hyperbolic space: Ric == -1*(m-1)*g
  [True] m=4, sphere: Ric == 1*(m-1)*g
  [True] m=4, hyperbolic space: Ric == -1*(m-1)*g

K1  variation formula (Lemma K1): at a point where delta = 0, with nabla = nabla^h,
    Ric(h+delta) - Ric(h) = (1/2) h^ad (nabla_a nabla_b delta_dc + nabla_a nabla_c delta_bd - nabla_a nabla_d delta_bc
      - nabla_b nabla_c delta_ad) - (1/2) h^ap h^dq nabla_a delta_pq T_dbc + (1/2) h^ap h^dq nabla_b delta_pq nabla_c delta_ad
      + (1/4) h^ap h^dq T_pad T_qbc - (1/4) h^ap h^dq T_pbd T_qac,   T_dbc = nabla_b delta_dc + nabla_c delta_db - nabla_d delta_bc.
    Test: random exact 2-jets of h and delta (delta(0) = 0), both Riccis by the independent routine.
  [True] m=2 sig=(2, 0): Ric(h+delta)-Ric(h) == formula (nabla^2 delta symmetric in its derivative slots: True; quadratic part != 0: True)
  [True] m=2 sig=(1, 1): Ric(h+delta)-Ric(h) == formula (nabla^2 delta symmetric in its derivative slots: True; quadratic part != 0: True)
  [True] m=3 sig=(3, 0): Ric(h+delta)-Ric(h) == formula (nabla^2 delta symmetric in its derivative slots: True; quadratic part != 0: True)
  [True] m=3 sig=(1, 2): Ric(h+delta)-Ric(h) == formula (nabla^2 delta symmetric in its derivative slots: True; quadratic part != 0: True)
  [True] m=4 sig=(2, 2): Ric(h+delta)-Ric(h) == formula (nabla^2 delta symmetric in its derivative slots: True; quadratic part != 0: True)
  [True] m=5 sig=(3, 2): Ric(h+delta)-Ric(h) == formula (nabla^2 delta symmetric in its derivative slots: True; quadratic part != 0: True)

K2  Lemma K2 on curved bases (random 3-jets, non-normal coordinates), Z2 at p = (0, g(0)) in s(X):
    (a) s_* = horizontal lift; (b) nabla pi_* = 0 at p, i.e. Gamma^{Z2,rho}_{ab}(p) = Gamma^{g,rho}_{ab}(0) for
    base directions a, b and 0 if a or b is vertical (A = 0 on s(X), T = 0); (c) nabla K at p has only the VV part
    (1/2)(U g^-1 W + W g^-1 U); (d) nabla delta, nabla^2 delta at p (adapted frame) are exactly those of K2;
    (e) fibre Christoffel symbols Gamma^F(U,W) = -(1/2)(U y^-1 W + W y^-1 U), independent of lambda.
  n=2 sig=(1, 1), g0 non-diagonal, Gamma_g(0) != 0: True, Ric_g(0) != 0: True; coefficients in Q(lam, cH, cV)   [0.5s]
  [True] n=2: (a) s_* = lift True; (b) nabla pi_* = 0 at p True; (c) nabla K at p True; (d) nabla delta, nabla^2 delta at p True; (e) fibre Christoffels True
  n=3 sig=(2, 1), g0 non-diagonal, Gamma_g(0) != 0: True, Ric_g(0) != 0: True; coefficients in Q(lam, cH, cV)   [7.7s]
  [True] n=3: (a) s_* = lift True; (b) nabla pi_* = 0 at p True; (c) nabla K at p True; (d) nabla delta, nabla^2 delta at p True; (e) fibre Christoffels True
  n=4 sig=(1, 3), g0 non-diagonal, Gamma_g(0) != 0: True, Ric_g(0) != 0: True; coefficients in Q(lam, cH, cV)   [35.5s]
  [True] n=4: (a) s_* = lift True; (b) nabla pi_* = 0 at p True; (c) nabla K at p True; (d) nabla delta, nabla^2 delta at p True; (e) fibre Christoffels True

K3  Lemma K3 (general n): the variation formula of K1 on the data of K2, by O(g)-invariant strand diagrams
    with symbolic loop weight n; coefficients in Q(n, lam, cH, cV), mu = lam/(1 - n lam).
  dRic_HH = (cH/(4*n*lam*cV - 4*cV)) g
  dRic_VV = (-1/4) G_0 + (0) tr(g^-1 .) tr(g^-1 .)
  dRic_HV: 0 diagrams (an H-V bilinear form has 3 endpoints, so no perfect matching exists)
  [True] dRic_HH == cH/(4 cV (n lam - 1)) g for every n
  [True] dRic_VV == -(1/4) G_0 for every n
  [True] dRic_HV == 0 for every n
  term-by-term (HH coefficient of g; VV coefficient of G_0, of tr tr):
    term 1: HH 0;  VV 0, 0
    term 2: HH 0;  VV 0, 0
    term 3: HH (-n**2*lam*cH - n*lam*cH + n*cH + 2*lam*cH + cH)/(4*n*lam*cV - 4*cV);  VV 0, 0
    term 4: HH 0;  VV -1/2, 0
    term 5: HH 0;  VV 0, 0
    term 6: HH 0;  VV 1/2, 0
    term 7: HH cH/(4*n*lam*cV - 4*cV);  VV 0, 0
    term 8: HH (n**2*lam*cH + n*lam*cH - n*cH - 2*lam*cH - cH)/(4*n*lam*cV - 4*cV);  VV -1/4, 0
  [True] C^V(X,Y) = -(cH/(2 cV)) [X^flat . Y^flat + mu g(X,Y) g]  (= II of F4(a))
  [True] fibre trace h^-1 . Ric_F = s_F = -n(n-1)(n+2)/(8 cV)
  [True] s_Y - R/cH = h^-1 . (Ric_F + dRic) == sigma_1/cV of F4(b)
  [True] -(n/4) G_{1/n} - (1/4) G_0 == -((n+1)/4) G_{1/(n+1)} (coefficients of G_0 and tr tr)
  engine cross-check: explicit h_p, nabla delta, nabla^2 delta in the adapted frame, n = 1..4:
  [True] n=1 sig=(0, 1): explicit evaluation == diagram evaluation at loop weight 1   [0.1s]
  [True] n=2 sig=(1, 1): explicit evaluation == diagram evaluation at loop weight 2   [0.3s]
  [True] n=3 sig=(3, 0): explicit evaluation == diagram evaluation at loop weight 3   [3.2s]
  [True] n=4 sig=(1, 3): explicit evaluation == diagram evaluation at loop weight 4   [13.0s]
  [True] VV block proportional to cV G_lam iff (kappa, lam) = [{kappa: -(n + 1)/(4*cV), lam: 1/(n + 1)}]; then Ric_g = (0) g  (F6, Z1 half)

